{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>First instance</b><br>כערוגת [like a bed]: a patch of ground in a garden." "מגדלות [towers]: from מגדל עז [Migdal-oz]." "<b>Second instance</b><br>לחייו [his cheeks]: the hair that is at their two ends, with him, מגדלות מרקחים [towering with spices]." "שושנים [lilies]: in goodness of fragrance." "<b>Third instance</b><br>לחייו [his cheeks]: [they are] the princes of the face." "שפתותיו [his lips]: they are his emissaries, the doers of his word, who speak with his prophets, like Gabriel (and) לבוש הבדים [clothed in linen]."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {4 "The bracketed [they are] reflects a supplied copula; the phrase שרי הפנים is a known epithet for angelic princes.", 5 "The vav prefixed to לבוש is marked parenthetically in the source; following 'Gabriel,' this alludes to Daniel 10:5 and/or Ezekiel 9–10, but the specific referent of the parenthetical vav is unclear."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:36.103120137Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}